bs -- Battleships=================    bs [-b | -s] [-c]Play the familiar Battleships game against the computer on a 10x10 board.Place your fleet on the Main Board, then hunt the computer's ships on theHit/Miss Board by firing at squares; the first to sink the other's wholefleet wins.  The interface is visual: move the cursor with the rogue/hackkeys h j k l y u b n (or the numeric keypad), and to fire, move to a squareand press any non-motion key.Placing ships: type the ship's capital letter to select it, move thecursor to where it should start, and a direction key to lay it down.  `r'places the current ship at random, `R' scatters all your remaining ships,and control-L redraws.  `-b' is a blitz (many shots a turn), `-s' thesalvo variant, `-c' lets ships touch.Original by Bruce Holloway; salvo option by Chuck A. DeGaul; userinterface, autoconfiguration and cleanup by Eric S. Raymond.  Posted toUsenet; carried here as posted.  Originals in SRC/bs/ORIG.